# Two Sum – One-Pass Hash Map (C++17)

> **Goal (paraphrased)**  
> Given an array `nums` and an integer `target`, return the **two distinct indices** *i, j* such that `nums[i] + nums[j] == target`. Exactly one valid pair is guaranteed.

---

## Intuition

* **Single scan → hash table.**  
  Each time we visit `nums[i]`, we know the value that would complete the pair:

  ```text
  need = target – nums[i]



class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> twoSum(const vector<int>& nums, int target) {
        unordered_map<int, int> indexOf;
        indexOf.reserve(nums.size());

        for (size_t i = 0; i < nums.size(); ++i) {
            int need = target - nums[i];
            if (auto it = indexOf.find(need); it != indexOf.end()) {
                return { static_cast<int>(it->second), static_cast<int>(i) };
            }
            indexOf[nums[i]] = static_cast<int>(i);
        }
    return {};
    }
};